hifiberry-audiocontrol (0.9.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * mpd: emit shuffle_changed and loop_mode_changed. The MPD controller
    subscribed to MPD's Options subsystem but its handler was a stub, so
    toggling shuffle or cycling the loop mode on the default player produced
    no WebSocket event at all - a client subscribed, waited, and nothing
    arrived. Options fires for any option change, consume and crossfade
    included, so the controller now holds the last-seen random/repeat/single
    and emits only on a real transition; the first observation after a
    connect establishes the baseline, so a reconnect does not look like
    someone toggling a setting.
  * postinst: chown /var/lib/audiocontrol recursively. Installs that at some
    point ran audiocontrol as root leave root-owned files under the cache
    directories, which the non-recursive chown did not fix, so the daemon
    still could not overwrite them after an upgrade. /etc/audiocontrol stays
    non-recursive: its dpkg conffiles, some shipped by other packages, remain
    root-owned.
  * control: accept libasound2t64 as an alternative to libasound2, so the
    dependency is satisfiable on trixie.
  * build.sh no longer sources the cross-compile environment; that setup is
    supplied by the surrounding OS build.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 04:03:45 +0000

hifiberry-audiocontrol (0.9.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * websocket: rename the outbound shuffle event from random_changed to
    shuffle_changed, matching the rest of the API, where the capability is
    "shuffle" and the inbound update event is already shuffle_changed. The
    old name meant a client subscribing to shuffle_changed - as the WebUI
    does, following the example in doc/websocket.md - never received the
    event at all, because subscriptions are filtered by exact event name.
    The event now carries both "shuffle" and the previous "enabled" field,
    and the subscription filter still accepts random_changed, so clients
    written against either name keep working.
  * doc/websocket.md described events that are not emitted and omitted five
    that are. Corrected against the implementation, including that
    position_changed sends a float rather than a {position, duration}
    object, that song_information_update is a partial update where an absent
    field means unchanged, and that source.player_id is built with a
    hardcoded MPD port and is wrong for other players.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Fri, 28 Aug 2026 17:52:00 +0000

hifiberry-audiocontrol (0.9.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * generic player: forward seek, set_loop_mode and set_shuffle to the
    external player's command_url instead of only updating local state, so
    the external player learns about seeks and loop/shuffle changes made
    through audiocontrol.
  * generic player: accept an inbound queue_changed API event to populate
    the player's queue.
  * generic player: interpolate playback position between position updates
    via PlayerProgress, so a bridge no longer needs to post position at 1 Hz.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:34:15 +0000

hifiberry-audiocontrol (0.8.9) trixie; urgency=medium

  * mpd: fall back to the album cover when a track has no cover art of its own.
    /library/mpd/image/<base64 track path> only asked MPD for the track's art,
    so an album whose files carry no embedded picture and whose directory holds
    no cover.jpg returned 404 - even when audiocontrol already had that album's
    cover in its image cache from an online lookup. The Now Playing page then
    showed a placeholder for such albums (typically WAV rips) while the very
    same artwork was served fine under /library/mpd/image/album:<id>. The track
    URL is now resolved to its album and the album cover is used as a fallback.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000

